{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1500752-understanding-liminals-and-getimians","id":1500752,"title":"Understanding Liminals and Getimians","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-01-19T11:58:51-08:00","id":1500752,"title":"Understanding Liminals and Getimians","content":"So, I've recently returned to the Exalted fold and decided the best way to approach 3rd Edition is to throw out everything I learned in the last 2 editions and start fresh. So I sat down a few days ago and started reading through the main rulebook right from the beginning.<br /> <br /> And while I appreciate and admire many of the small and subtle changes made so far, I find myself scratching my head at the emergence of the three new types of Exalt, and I was wondering if you guys could help me understand them a little more.<br /> <br /> I mean, to be honest though, the Exigent Exalts aren't *really* all that hard to understand - both in and out of game. We have all had those players who just - for whatever reason - don't identify with the Lunar/Solar/DB/Abyssal/Sidereal structure and/or they can't bring themselves to color inside the lines and it's probably a good idea to have them Exalted *from* the little gods rather than make them spirits or little Gods themselves. In the end, I would prefer that in a game like Exalted, people be *some* sort of Exalt. So that's cool. Not too much real mystery there.<br /> <br /> Now we go on the the Liminals, who I can wrap my head around conceptually - I think. These are beings who've been cobbled together physically from different bodies and are supposed to...there I get a bit fuzzy. Can someone tell me (like you were explaining it to a complete dunce) What the LIminal are meant to do and (if anybody knows) what was the idea *behind* their creation? Were they originally created to fill some sort of niche in the current ecosystem of Creation? Some gap in the original five-fold order?<br /> <br /> And if the Liminal Exalted are somewhat mystifying to me, the Getimian's current information borders on good old fashioned Borgstromancy. Exalts who dwell in constant awareness of realities that never came to be? Sounds really tragic - but what do they *do*? And more to the point, why did somebody decide Creation needed them? Again, does anybody have any insight into the Dev's motivation for including them?<br /> <br /> I'm not hostile to new Exalts per se - it's just that I can explain All the other Exalts to new players in One sentence - maybe two - and those sentences won't be really complicated per se. As it stands now, I'm not sure I can do that with The Liminals and Getimians and I was hoping you guys could help me with that.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21614-corradus","name":"Corradus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21614_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-19T13:24:11-08:00","id":1500766,"title":"","content":"Liminals and Getimian were originally envisioned as foils for Abyssals and Sidereals respectively to highlight aspects of those splats that had previously been ignored.<br /> <br /> Sidereals had been subsumed by their faction conflict and it was unclear how they maintained fate or what would happen if they stopped and Abyssals, despite having the Underworld as a place of strength had little reason to ever go there. Like individual Storytellers could find their own answers for these problems but that still didn't address that the general shape of their games tended towards the stories that involved other Exalts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-19T22:56:21-08:00","id":1500816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Corradus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1500752-understanding-liminals-and-getimians#post1500752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...<br /> I mean, to be honest though, the Exigent Exalts aren't *really* all that hard to understand - both in and out of game. We have all had those players who just - for whatever reason - don't identify with the Lunar/Solar/DB/Abyssal/Sidereal structure and/or they can't bring themselves to color inside the lines and it's probably a good idea to have them Exalted *from* the little gods rather than make them spirits or little Gods themselves. In the end, I would prefer that in a game like Exalted, people be *some* sort of Exalt. So that's cool. Not too much real mystery there.</div> </div> </div> </div>To expand on them a bit. Folks did like things like Devil Tigers in Infernals, but it kind of created a situation where it actively detracted from Infenrals (as it suddenly becmae the Be Another Exalt theme than really dobulingd own on well, Hell themes). And it creates a bit of a bridge for homebrewers between a Martial Arts style and a full-on splat ala Dragon-Blooded or Solars. I'd say at least these are kind of as important as the other bits you mention.<br /> <br /> Basically having a Misc. Category Exalts is generally like, a good practice.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Corradus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1500752-understanding-liminals-and-getimians#post1500752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now we go on the the Liminals, who I can wrap my head around conceptually - I think. These are beings who've been cobbled together physically from different bodies and are supposed to...there I get a bit fuzzy. Can someone tell me (like you were explaining it to a complete dunce) What the LIminal are meant to do and (if anybody knows) what was the idea *behind* their creation? Were they originally created to fill some sort of niche in the current ecosystem of Creation? Some gap in the original five-fold order?</div> </div> </div> </div>Liminals have a couple reasons they exist. I'm going to go over what <i>they are</i> in character first (the Watsonian take). And then go over why they are out of character (the Doylist take).<br /> <br /> So, in-setting, the origins of Liminals is still kind of vague. We know form what is in the text and dev comments that a Liminal is what happens when someone tries to bring someone back from the dead, and gets something else isntead. The corpse animates, gets powers, and is bound to the creator and its instinctive needs to interact with death and the dead. The body is not the perosn brought back to life. Their souls have moved on. They are the meat animated again and imbued with a new conciousness and Exaltation. What awakens them is something we only know as the Dark Mother, an entity that exists in what the Underworld was before the titans found it and made it what it is in relation to Creation.<br /> <br /> A bit of a difference of understanding the Underworld is that in 3e it is not something that came to being when the things that became the Neverborn died. It was there in some form before history began, but what that was, exactly, is nto clear. There's actually a bit of fiction hinting at this in 1e, where the Underworld was like a spoider's web where a fly crashes into it, twists it up, and it no longer a web. The Underworld as it is <i>is managled</i>. And notably: What happened to the spider? They first showed-up around the Shogunate, after the rise of the Deathlords. And kind of instincutlaly try to keep order in the line of life and death. So destroying hungry ghosts, hunting especially mean necromancers, or serving as a bridge between death and life as best they can.<br /> <br /> The out-of-character aspects are a fewfold. First, simply, the devs of late 2e wer given the challenge to create Prometheans (ala Chronicles of Darkness) in Creation. So they draw on the similar idea of being beings created from failed ressurection and the disassociation of body and mind that pertains to. That's like, the simplest bt. They are to Created like Lunars are to Fera or Abyssals to Kindred. Notably, though they <i>do fork</i> pretty hard from there, much like the other splats do.You see this in their kind of &quot;play loop&quot;. While a Promethean is trying to find hunaity thorugh their alchemcial Refinements, Liminals are creatures both alive and dead trying to bridge the gap between them. They're much more &quot;necromantic&quot; in theems and aesthetic than I feel Created are.<br /> <br /> The other Doylist thing going on in the setting is kind of focus. Something 3e made a point of with splats (though admittedly I feel not clealry with Solars) was to make sure that while they are broad, they are still nailed-down in a few themes. So for example, Lunar Exalted are shapeshifters, and are great at it. But they're <i>a particular kind of shapeshifter</i>. Notably they turn into human and animals. They don't turn into rocks, they don't do Reed Richards stretching, and so on. There are things in setting that can do that, but Lunars aren't trying ot be every single &quot;shapeshifter&quot; trope. Instead, they are a set of clear ones.<br /> <br /> Now Abyssals actually did have the &quot;All undead stuff under the sun&quot; to them. They ahd vampiric, zombie, revenant, lich, specter, and all that. THey were the liminal ones who were both alive and dead who straddled th eline. But htey alsow ere badass necromancer overlords. They were beatiful vampires or lich monsters....and also flesh-eating cannibals and splatterpunk. And notably, all of this was couched in their general &quot;heel&quot; qualities of being dark, edgy expression of Solar power. While also being really the only splat that like...gave a shit to interact with the Undewrold in anything but an antagonistic light. And even then....were in a sort of antaongistic light anyhow. So in this context, Liminals do a couple htings.<br /> <br /> First, they kind of give more angles to approach the Underworld with. They're for play on par with Dragon-Blooded, so while powerful, less world-shattering. They allow going into depth about how the unique way death and dying work in Creaiton's setting. And due to being more in the well, meditaor role, can do so while having to worry about its threats and its alienness with a bit of a &quot;playing by their terms&quot; feel than the usual Abyssal dominaiton of these things. It also presents angles foa n Underworld that can be dangerous but not necessarily hostile. THis allows Abyssals, in contrast, to double-down on well, their strengths. Being Death's Lawgivers, serving the powers of the Deathlords, and generally haivng the &quot;Badass wearing balck&quot; things more as their thing. They can still do the reflecitve on life and eath and mediator stuff, but it's a differnece in being a dominating power versus inbetween guy.<br /> <br /> The second is actually powerwise. Liminals kind of offload a lot of the splatterpunk, body horror, and gore stuff of Abysslas into a new context that turns out you can build a whole splat of powers out of. And still be left with the themes of Power, Shadow, Death, Darkness, and all the other Badass Dark Lord stuff that Abyssals had going. It allows Abyssals to have a focused, clearer set of themes, and the things they couldn't quite touch could still be picked-up and explored with Liminals.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Corradus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1500752-understanding-liminals-and-getimians#post1500752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And if the Liminal Exalted are somewhat mystifying to me, the Getimian's current information borders on good old fashioned Borgstromancy. Exalts who dwell in constant awareness of realities that never came to be? Sounds really tragic - but what do they *do*? And more to the point, why did somebody decide Creation needed them? Again, does anybody have any insight into the Dev's motivation for including them?...</div> </div> </div> </div>The Watsonian take is basically their creators tried something weird, it got weird, they didn't like it. The basic way they interact with things is yeha, they never were born. Their Origin never happened. It's likebeing in <i>It's a Wonderful Life</i> and you'll never get to go to the good reality where you mattered, saved the town, and were important. You were robbed of your existance and you see the consequences of that. As to what you do, the options they show are a fewfold. Try to make things rihgt. You could do it again. Or make it so it always was enough if you push things enough. You can fight Heaven for revenge. Or do things to get back what's yours. Or you can just kind of accept your new fate and see what you can do with what wasn't there with cool glitch magic.<br /> <br /> The why they are out of character is a few things. Originally, it was to give Sidereals a bit something clearer in the sense of outright enemy sabotage story, versus the incidental Lunar or Solar hostiltiy through on the ground stuff. A peer Exalt that was a foil in the sense of something that played in the same high concept space Sidereals mess with and directly attacking wht Sidereals carea bout in a cool Fighting Over Reality thing. They have Daoist and alchemy themes too con contrast with the Sidereals astrologer and Journey to the West stuff. Shaolin v. Wutang. MI6 v. Specter. Those sort of things.<br /> <br /> Originally the prior devs didn't plan much save them being kind of a weird NPC splat that you used for that War in Heaven stuff. But the current devs saw th epotential of a full Circle of Getimians and so developed them out. THey still have some inherent foil with Sidereals, but due to how they are also about upheavla and kind of being spooky reality-warpers and a bit of a revoutionary vibe, do have fun potential in interactions wiht Solars, Lunars, or Dragon-Blooded too. So they fleshed them out more fully into a full splat we know now. They honeslty to me are the most &quot;superfluous&quot; Exalt in that the setting probably didn't like, <i>need</i> them per se. But htey're pretty cool I think for just allowing cool powers and themes other Exalts don't. Notably the reality-bending in ways that are a bit more outright about &quot;ripping relaity apart and doing screwy to it in ways that are unnerving&quot; versus Sidereals &quot;I know the weird secrest sand use the rules that are there, just obscure&quot; things.<br /> <br /> For all three new Exalts, there's also a bit with how to an extent, there was a want to break-up Exaltation to be Celesital Exalted + Dragon-Blooded. ANd then Alchemicals, who were this weird &quot;Not the prior cateogires, gbut Celetail Exalted of mechanics that care becuase no one wants to be a DB.&quot; Liminals and Getimians having very not-Celestial origins helps breaks things up. Exigents having the variety of implmentaitons does that further. It helps make Exaltation more diverse by well....bieng more diverse with Exaltation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-20T14:19:44-08:00","id":1500867,"title":"","content":"Wow Blaque, thank you. That helped a lot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21614-corradus","name":"Corradus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21614_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-20T17:41:45-08:00","id":1500887,"title":"","content":"On a little aside, speaking of &quot;XX is what happens when someone tries to bring someone back from the dead, and gets something else instead&quot; reminded of FMA's Homunculi and now i ask myself how much would they actually mesh or clash with Liminals themes.<br /> <br /> Or maybe some sort of analog to Pandorans from PtC, perhaps. Just randomly musing\u200b really,<br /> <br /> <br /> Plus, it reminded of a little bit of 2e lore that could be a very interesting monkeywrench of sorts to games with or without Liminals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 01-20-2023, 08:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-20T17:52:09-08:00","id":1500890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1500752-understanding-liminals-and-getimians?p=1500887#post1500887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Possibly also of some analog to Pandorans from PtC, too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, in my game I've established that sometimes one of the Neverborn or a Hekatonkhire answers when there's a resurrection attempt and the result isn't pretty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-20T18:01:48-08:00","id":1500891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1500752-understanding-liminals-and-getimians?p=1500890#post1500890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, in my game I've established that sometimes one of the Neverborn or a Hekatonkhire answers when there's a resurrection attempt and the result isn't pretty.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds fun, tempts me considerably to mess around with adapting Prometheans' Disquiet mechanics (though i guess Abyssal Ressonance is close aplenty as it was).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-21T01:45:12-08:00","id":1500909,"title":"","content":"If Liminal Exalted are inspired by Promethean then I think that for the moment the closest thing that they have to Pandorans is what becomes of them if they do not have a living person with whom they have that profound spiritual connection.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-21T07:42:23-08:00","id":1500937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1500752-understanding-liminals-and-getimians?p=1500909#post1500909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Liminal Exalted are inspired by Promethean then I think that for the moment the closest thing that they have to Pandorans is what becomes of them if they do not have a living person with whom they have that profound spiritual connection.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Good point - has there been any discussion of the kind of changes this causes in the Liminal and their potential as antagonists?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-21T11:49:26-08:00","id":1500953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1500752-understanding-liminals-and-getimians?p=1500937#post1500937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good point - has there been any discussion of the kind of changes this causes in the Liminal and their potential as antagonists?</div> </div> </div> </div>Only in the Essence manuscript. If they lose that connection, whether through neglect, resolution, or death of the living person, all living creatures start to shun them instinctively, and the following occurs:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Decomposition reduces the Liminal to a shambling corpse or hungry ghost within one lunar month. They lose another Intimacy per week, and can no longer use Undying [their ability to resurrect as long as their brain is intact]. They also decompose cosmetically, per the player\u2019s aesthetic choice. The Liminal can still anchor her Thread of Life to a mortal within this time. If she does, decomposition stops and she heals. Liminals of Essence 3+ may anchor themselves to an Exalt within their Circle, or to another powerful entity. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-21T13:26:47-08:00","id":1500960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1500752-understanding-liminals-and-getimians?p=1500953#post1500953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Only in the Essence manuscript. If they lose that connection, whether through neglect, resolution, or death of the living person, all living creatures start to shun them instinctively, and the following occurs:<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The fact that <i>resolution</i> of that connection can have the same consequences as neglect or death of the living person, that is peculiar indeed, as an aside, something to explore the implications of in the future perhaps.<br /> <br /> Hmmm, looking like the loss of an anchor makes them degenerate, not only mentally but possibly in a power level perspective too, as the loss of the Undying capacity itself seems to imply the &quot;reduction to a shambling corpse or hungry ghost&quot; of liminals that stay &quot;untethered&quot; beyond the lunar month limit might be farther than skin deep.<br /> <br /> <br /> Damn, now i'm having the terrible, horrible idea of a group of veteran liminals manipulated/brainwashed/tricked into becoming the honor guard/harem/etc of a funeral god, Nephwrack, Abyssal or other high powered possible necromancer. Ok, that's some definite antagonist fodder to tinker with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 07-18-2025, 09:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-21T18:24:27-08:00","id":1500986,"title":"","content":"As an aside, the idea of Mother Bog and her children crafted of corpses parts, mud, wood and sorcery having some form of connection fallen Liminals or the Dark Mother herself just crossed my mind. Worth hitting the books to brainstorm things i guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-21T19:31:46-08:00","id":1500995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1500752-understanding-liminals-and-getimians?p=1500986#post1500986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As an aside, the idea of Mother Bog and her children crafted of corpses parts, mud, wood and sorcery having some form of connection fallen Liminals or the Dark Mother herself just crossed my mind. Worth hitting the books to brainstorm things i guess.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would expect that she has ended up creating a Liminal or two over the centuries, even if it wasn't on purpose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-21T23:55:58-08:00","id":1501012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1500752-understanding-liminals-and-getimians?p=1500960#post1500960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fact that <i>resolution</i> of that connection can have the same consequences as neglect or death of the living person, that is peculiar indeed, as an aside, something to explore the implications of in the future perhaps.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Mm. There's a line in the Essence Liminals writeup that if a Liminal's connection is abusive, then breaking that connection through healing has the same effect as neglect/death, which I summarised as 'resolution'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-22T01:56:24-08:00","id":1501016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1500752-understanding-liminals-and-getimians?p=1500995#post1500995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would expect that she has ended up creating a Liminal or two over the centuries, even if it wasn't on purpose.</div> </div> </div> </div>What Aspect would they be?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-22T06:04:47-08:00","id":1501026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1500752-understanding-liminals-and-getimians?p=1501012#post1501012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mm. There's a line in the Essence Liminals writeup that if a Liminal's connection is abusive, then breaking that connection through healing has the same effect as neglect/death, which I summarised as 'resolution'.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for clearing that up. Really should take some time to read Essence myself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-07T02:05:34-08:00","id":1502368,"title":"","content":"As far as Exigents go my group has been playing them more or less like Varients from the Loki series, they grew up thinking that their world was the real one and now they find themselves in a twisted version of creation. They generally either try to get back (impossible as they didn't actually come from anywhere else but they don't know that) or make this world more liek the one they knew. In an essence game I played the leader of a slave revolt in Gem who was horrified to elarn that the despot hadn't been overththrown in this reality and dedicated themselves to that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9124-satoshi","name":"satoshi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-07T12:10:50-08:00","id":1502409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>satoshi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1500752-understanding-liminals-and-getimians?p=1502368#post1502368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as Exigents go my group has been playing them more or less like Varients from the Loki series, they grew up thinking that their world was the real one and now they find themselves in a twisted version of creation. They generally either try to get back (impossible as they didn't actually come from anywhere else but they don't know that) or make this world more liek the one they knew. In an essence game I played the leader of a slave revolt in Gem who was horrified to elarn that the despot hadn't been overththrown in this reality and dedicated themselves to that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you meant Getimians, not Exigents?<br /> <br /> On the subject of Getimians, they kinda are the isekai Exalts. They are not real or native to &quot;Official&quot; Creation. Their &quot;creation&quot; is tied to 2 Primordials/Yozi (Oramus &quot;I Am the Abyss from M:Aw&quot; and Sacheverell &quot;I dream of the Future and people think I will preDestiny Trap everyone if/when I wake&quot;). There isn't a lot known about them beyond that.<br /> I don't even know if they are limited to mortals in their prior lives. I'm considering pulling out a Gunstar Siderial and undergoing the conversion process because I think it would be an entertaining story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-10T10:13:53-08:00","id":1502698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1500752-understanding-liminals-and-getimians?p=1500816#post1500816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They are to Created like Lunars are to Fera or Abyssals to Kindred. Notably, though they <i>do fork</i> pretty hard from there, much like the other splats do.You see this in their kind of &quot;play loop&quot;. While a Promethean is trying to find hunaity thorugh their alchemcial Refinements, Liminals are creatures both alive and dead trying to bridge the gap between them. They're much more &quot;necromantic&quot; in theems and aesthetic than I feel Created are.</div> </div> </div> </div> So, fun fact:<br /> <br /> Holden has been putting out an &quot;Exalted demake,&quot; which is to say, Exalted rendered in oWoD 20th anniversary mechanics. I happened to snag his preview of Liminals, built on the same ideas that went into the old Kickstarter preview -- Liminals as they were to be, rather than how they will be -- and they're really just Prometheans.<br /> <br /> Though they are hunters of the dead and aligned with the Underworld, they also have pretty half-cocked alchemical theming (mostly arbitrary alchemical terms in various Charm names) and a mechanic and play loop for &quot;the Journey&quot; to leave the Liminal condition behind, becoming instead a mortal or a personal kind of Exalted.<br /> <br /> I suspect the new writing team are going to take them in a different direction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-10T13:16:04-08:00","id":1502705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1500752-understanding-liminals-and-getimians?p=1502698#post1502698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> So, fun fact:<br /> <br /> Holden has been putting out an &quot;Exalted demake,&quot; which is to say, Exalted rendered in oWoD 20th anniversary mechanics. I happened to snag his preview of Liminals, built on the same ideas that went into the old Kickstarter preview -- Liminals as they were to be, rather than how they will be -- and they're really just Prometheans.<br /> <br /> Though they are hunters of the dead and aligned with the Underworld, they also have pretty half-cocked alchemical theming (mostly arbitrary alchemical terms in various Charm names) and a mechanic and play loop for &quot;the Journey&quot; to leave the Liminal condition behind, becoming instead a mortal or a personal kind of Exalted.<br /> <br /> I suspect the new writing team are going to take them in a different direction.</div> </div> </div> </div>From what Vance has said, the main Liminal story-space is the search for identity - they're created not knowing who they are, their bodies and their memories from other people, and they have to work through that, put together an identity for themselves and decide what they want. I've not seen any intimation of them aiming to become something metaphysically different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-10T14:26:59-08:00","id":1502711,"title":"","content":"As long as they know what to do with them, I'm happy (extending or cutting the one-month countdown on untethered Liminals is a bonus).<br /> <br /> Really, after WFHW, I was dreading future Liminal mechanics. After seeing the Terrestial-level Charms in Exigents, I'm feeling a lot better about them. Now I just need them to exist in a timely manner. I've got Gut's Theme to play on blast and ridiculous splatterpunk stunts to make.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-11T05:42:47-08:00","id":1502743,"title":"","content":"It's mostly Exalted Essence that's made me optimistic for Liminals.<br /> <br /> I didn't dislike them before, but their aspects make more sense to me now whereas before they felt like they had them because they were the first of the new exalt types conceptually and the developers decided they needed to subdivide into 5 castes/aspects in order to be accepted as a new Exalt type by the fanbase rather than because they were necessary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-11T08:56:01-08:00","id":1502755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1500752-understanding-liminals-and-getimians?p=1502409#post1502409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you meant Getimians, not Exigents?<br /> <br /> On the subject of Getimians, they kinda are the isekai Exalts. They are not real or native to &quot;Official&quot; Creation. Their &quot;creation&quot; is tied to 2 Primordials/Yozi (Oramus &quot;I Am the Abyss from M:Aw&quot; and Sacheverell &quot;I dream of the Future and people think I will preDestiny Trap everyone if/when I wake&quot;). There isn't a lot known about them beyond that.<br /> I don't even know if they are limited to mortals in their prior lives. I'm considering pulling out a Gunstar Siderial and undergoing the conversion process because I think it would be an entertaining story.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that in the Realm there's a lone Getimian that is implied to have been a Dragon-Blooded Dynast and prefect in its &quot;reality of origin&quot; (if memory tricks me not), so your idea might not be all that far-fetched.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-11T09:45:27-08:00","id":1502760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1500752-understanding-liminals-and-getimians?p=1502743#post1502743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's mostly Exalted Essence that's made me optimistic for Liminals.<br /> <br /> I didn't dislike them before, but their aspects make more sense to me now whereas before they felt like they had them because they were the first of the new exalt types conceptually and the developers decided they needed to subdivide into 5 castes/aspects in order to be accepted as a new Exalt type by the fanbase rather than because they were necessary.</div> </div> </div> </div> Personally, I'm hoping they broaden the Aspects by the time they get a splatbook. Breath in particular seems oddly narrow -- the preview from the old KS included despair among their birthing passions, and I'm not sure where the &quot;punish the wicked&quot; things comes from -- and the Aspect markings feel really prescriptive compared to Dragon-Blooded ones.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1500752-understanding-liminals-and-getimians?p=1502755#post1502755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that in the Realm there's a lone Getimian that is implied to have been a Dragon-Blooded Dynast and prefect in its &quot;reality of origin&quot; (if memory tricks me not), so your idea might not be all that far-fetched.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div> I think he's meant to be a mortal scion of a lost House; there's nothing that suggests he was Exalted before he was real.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-11T11:52:29-08:00","id":1502764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1500752-understanding-liminals-and-getimians?p=1502755#post1502755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that in the Realm there's a lone Getimian that is implied to have been a Dragon-Blooded Dynast and prefect in its &quot;reality of origin&quot; (if memory tricks me not), so your idea might not be all that far-fetched.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>The Getimian option for the Chanos Flicker in <i>The Realm</i> has him as a mortal merchant who belonged to House Chanos, which's... a bit different from your memory.<br /> <br /> Vance's said that while you can say a Getimian was another type of Exalted in their Origin, it's not the canonical presentation (the setting generally not allowing being two types of Exalted, or changing from one type to an unrelated type),","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-11T14:32:35-08:00","id":1502772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1500752-understanding-liminals-and-getimians?p=1502764#post1502764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Getimian option for the Chanos Flicker in <i>The Realm</i> has him as a mortal merchant who belonged to House Chanos, which's... a bit different from your memory.<br /> <br /> Vance's said that while you can say a Getimian was another type of Exalted in their Origin, it's not the canonical presentation (the setting generally not allowing being two types of Exalted, or changing from one type to an unrelated type),</div> </div> </div> </div>That in turn, gets very close to implying that the Sidereal position that Getimians don't actually exist prior Exaltation is objectively wrong. That the worlds they come from are real, not merely the path not taken. It is very close to &quot;Exalted Multiverse confirmed&quot;, which in turn is a stone's throw away from one of the big forbidden capacities in Exalted. Specifically, time travel. It is not, but it could be used to basically the same effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-11T17:36:05-08:00","id":1502793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1500752-understanding-liminals-and-getimians?p=1500816#post1500816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Originally the prior devs didn't plan much save them being kind of a weird NPC splat that you used for that War in Heaven stuff. But the current devs saw th epotential of a full Circle of Getimians and so developed them out. THey still have some inherent foil with Sidereals, but due to how they are also about upheavla and kind of being spooky reality-warpers and a bit of a revoutionary vibe, do have fun potential in interactions wiht Solars, Lunars, or Dragon-Blooded too. So they fleshed them out more fully into a full splat we know now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh. This is the first I'd heard of that. I mean, I'd heard that castes were definitely a contribution of the new devs, but if one of the three new Exalted types 3e first pitched to us were just NPC antagonists I would have been disappointed<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-12T01:25:43-08:00","id":1502814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1500752-understanding-liminals-and-getimians?p=1502772#post1502772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That in turn, gets very close to implying that the Sidereal position that Getimians don't actually exist prior Exaltation is objectively wrong. That the worlds they come from are real, not merely the path not taken. It is very close to &quot;Exalted Multiverse confirmed&quot;, which in turn is a stone's throw away from one of the big forbidden capacities in Exalted. Specifically, time travel. It is not, but it could be used to basically the same effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's the relevant quote from the fan Discord:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As a general proposition, the setting doesn't allow being two types of Exalted, or changing from one type of Exalt to another, and it's something where the canonical presentation of the setting does not invite people to do clever end runs around it. &quot;Ah, but a Getimian who remembers being a Solar wasn't actually a Solar!&quot; is an endrun that might work at your table but it is not something that we'll be presenting as how things canonically work. </div> </div> </div>(yadda yadda Solar-Abyssal yadda yadda 'general proposition')","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-12T04:03:37-08:00","id":1502821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1500752-understanding-liminals-and-getimians?p=1502743#post1502743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's mostly Exalted Essence that's made me optimistic for Liminals.<br /> <br /> I didn't dislike them before, but their aspects make more sense to me now whereas before they felt like they had them because they were the first of the new exalt types conceptually and the developers decided they needed to subdivide into 5 castes/aspects in order to be accepted as a new Exalt type by the fanbase rather than because they were necessary.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh, I've not read Essence. What did it give Blood, Bone, Flesh, Marrow, and Soil that they didn't have before that makes them feel suitable as Aspects for corpse Exalted?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-12T10:55:36-08:00","id":1502857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1500752-understanding-liminals-and-getimians?p=1502821#post1502821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Huh, I've not read Essence. What did it give Blood, Bone, Flesh, Marrow, and Soil that they didn't have before that makes them feel suitable as Aspects for corpse Exalted?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a mechanic called Nature which is similar to Aura in that you do some action to cause you to enter it. And while in it, you will get benefits to some of your Aspect powers as well. A lot of flavor space and distinction lives there. The actual Aspects also have some good characterization there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-12T11:00:22-08:00","id":1502858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1500752-understanding-liminals-and-getimians?p=1502772#post1502772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That in turn, gets very close to implying that the Sidereal position that Getimians don't actually exist prior Exaltation is objectively wrong. That the worlds they come from are real, not merely the path not taken. It is very close to &quot;Exalted Multiverse confirmed&quot;, which in turn is a stone's throw away from one of the big forbidden capacities in Exalted. Specifically, time travel. It is not, but it could be used to basically the same effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see how.<br /> <br /> The Origin is bascially like, a simulation. it is some mortal who did something intersting which would have been worth putting a Destiny to. Plenty of mortals are parts of interesting Destinies in Creation. And some of those are just never born as the Destiny is discarded. Destinies don't predict or account for Exaltations. They <i>can't</i>. So Destinies (which are ultimlatley what is the thing a Getimian is) don't have Exaltation as part of their narrative plan really.<br /> <br /> LIke, the devs have said a few times the Origin never happens. You can interpret it as that, but the text is probably going to be pretty clear come Getimians the main thing is your Destiny never happend, you were never born. And a thing in 3e in general is mortals can do impressive shit. You only ever lived as, ultimately, a potential forecast on the super calculator that is the Loom. And they went with Option A while leaving you on the wayside.<br /> <br /> Note also that the ones who created your Exaltation are titans amounting to Laplace's Demon and a being who Can See all the Waveform. I tend to think ever Getimain who will Exalt already has been Chosen. It's just you know, way back when through weird forward-looking probablity shit. The Ancients e weird, yo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-12T17:17:34-08:00","id":1502897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1500752-understanding-liminals-and-getimians?p=1502821#post1502821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh, I've not read Essence. What did it give Blood, Bone, Flesh, Marrow, and Soil that they didn't have before that makes them feel suitable as Aspects for corpse Exalted?</div> </div> </div> </div> While I'm not a fan of the ExEss Breath Aspects, the old KS writeups were more about the symbolism of and justifications for the Aspects rather than the kinds of characters they represent, while the ExEss ones have the benefit of Aspect-specific anima powers and experience conditions to suggest archetypes.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-12T18:20:31-08:00","id":1502905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1500752-understanding-liminals-and-getimians?p=1502857#post1502857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's a mechanic called Nature which is similar to Aura in that you do some action to cause you to enter it. And while in it, you will get benefits to some of your Aspect powers as well. A lot of flavor space and distinction lives there. The actual Aspects also have some good characterization there.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. Additionally the Ghost-Hunter QC in the Ex3 core was IMO a bit too physical for the first Liminal we ever saw and left me unclear what their charms did besides body horror.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-13T15:44:30-08:00","id":1502965,"title":"","content":"I suppose I misread the statement about Aspects making more sense as being more in terms of &quot;they don't seem to be fitting&quot; rather than knowing what could be done with them.<br /> <br /> Although I'll at least defend that misreading on the grounds that it seemed to make the most sense with the point about calling them perfunctory.<br /> <br /> That being said, some of the response does leave me a little concerned that it ended up with a write-up that kind of inclines them back towards a hazier distinction with Caste.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-13T16:04:09-08:00","id":1502967,"title":"","content":"Getimians who were Exalts in their Origin seem like they are going to have the same energy as Lunars with a something like a Storm Serpent as their spirit shape, probably not going to unbalance anything but it's probably not a good sign.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>success is the ability to go from one failure to the next without any loss of enthusiasm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1115-the-hug-ninja","name":"The Hug Ninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1115_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"324"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-14T07:45:41-08:00","id":1503029,"title":"","content":"I'd be leery of it. For one the concept of &quot;I used to have one power suite, now I have a potentially completely unrelated one &quot; feels like an awkward thing to play.<br /> <br /> For another, honestly bigger issue: this may not be as big a deal if it's just one Getimian among others, but it plays into an old conceit that the game has tried to discard: the idea that mortals don't matter or have significant narrative agency unless and until they Exalt. One of the former devs, I believe, described Exaltation as &quot;becoming the hero you always were.&quot;<br /> <br /> These may be my own concerns that aren't broadly shared, and that's fine. But I did want to put it out there","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-15T06:11:36-08:00","id":1503135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1500752-understanding-liminals-and-getimians?p=1502793#post1502793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh. This is the first I'd heard of that. I mean, I'd heard that castes were definitely a contribution of the new devs, but if one of the three new Exalted types 3e first pitched to us were just NPC antagonists I would have been disappointed</div> </div> </div> </div>Think the same initial word count as one of the Apocryphals in Exigents, John once used the Dragon King section of the Player's Guide as a point of reference which is about the same size.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-17T17:55:04-08:00","id":1503351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Hug Ninja</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1500752-understanding-liminals-and-getimians?p=1502967#post1502967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Getimians who were Exalts in their Origin seem like they are going to have the same energy as Lunars with a something like a Storm Serpent as their spirit shape, probably not going to unbalance anything but it's probably not a good sign.</div> </div> </div> </div>I remember that there was an Alchemical in 2nd ed that was a Solar in his previous incarnation, and even remembered his old life. If that didn't break the world then, a 'fictitious' existence as a DB on a non-existent life would not break now. If the overwhelming majority of the Getimians were mortal, having them (not really) been 'exalted' once or twice won't be a big problem, IMO. You could even have them coming from exaltations that never existed or that currently do not exist (that could get a good campaign seed that would be hard to do otherwise - 'I was an Auroral and now there are no Aurorals, why?' so this takes to investigating proscribed information about exalted, then about the Hearteaters, and so on).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-17T19:19:39-08:00","id":1503352,"title":"","content":"You mean <i>Luminous Exarch</i> one of the eight original Autocthonian Alchemicals who felt entitled to take over the world because of his memories of being a Solar? Yeeeeah, I'd be a bit concerned if that was the premise for someone's PC in an Alchemicals game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>success is the ability to go from one failure to the next without any loss of enthusiasm","edited":{"userid":1115,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1115-the-hug-ninja","user":"The Hug Ninja","date":". 02-18-2023, 11:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1115-the-hug-ninja","name":"The Hug Ninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1115_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"324"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-17T23:19:30-08:00","id":1503357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontop</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1500752-understanding-liminals-and-getimians?p=1503351#post1503351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I remember that there was an Alchemical in 2nd ed that was a Solar in his previous incarnation, and even remembered his old life. If that didn't break the world then, a 'fictitious' existence as a DB on a non-existent life would not break now. If the overwhelming majority of the Getimians were mortal, having them (not really) been 'exalted' once or twice won't be a big problem, IMO. You could even have them coming from exaltations that never existed or that currently do not exist (that could get a good campaign seed that would be hard to do otherwise - 'I was an Auroral and now there are no Aurorals, why?' so this takes to investigating proscribed information about exalted, then about the Hearteaters, and so on).</div> </div> </div> </div>The context is differenc mostly since <i>Luminous Exarch</i>, Estasia, and the unnamed Solar past life were still like, separate people. It's vague memoreis and such, but Estasia didn't get anything out of it and <i>Exarch</i> himself mostly used it for ego, but he was still ultimatley a different person just like every Alchemical incarnation is a different person.<br /> <br /> Like, kind of simlarly one could get a Liminal via the corpse of a Solar or something. It's still not hte Solar and not really going to be expected to get anything out of it, since the Exaltation and souls and such is gone. It's the meat the guy was made out of given a new existence.<br /> <br /> The Getimian whent hey Exalt <i>are that person</i>. A person that never was, but it kind of is a bit different since it's not like the former Solar reborn as <i>Exarch</i>. It's <i>Exarch</i> using a legacy someone else their soul use to be to justify his title of Twice Exalted Ig uess.<br /> <br /> And again, as we know of 3e metaphysics and goals, kind fo to me is just not fitting. Again, a big thing with Getimians are built on:<br /> 1) Mortals can be heroic. The lack of mechanical oomph to them is mostly a mistake of not relying on QCs harder, and the system isn't physics nayhow. They don't need to be Exalted to do impressive stuff.<br /> <br /> 2) Destinies aren't written for Exalts. Heaven can't dictate an Exalt will be there for htem to be fulfilled, so won't be writing destinies (discarded or otherwise) that assume Exalts.<br /> <br /> 3) Every other Exalt in general tries to avoid the double-dipping rule. Getimians, even with their nature, are not going to likely break this explicilty.<br /> <br /> LIke, the responded-to-post I think still matters here. Double-Exalts are like storm serpent Lunars or full on isekai Getimians. Do what you will, but it's not something I think the setting will assume by default and not be written assuming as possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-18T08:58:07-08:00","id":1503380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1500752-understanding-liminals-and-getimians?p=1503357#post1503357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">LIke, the responded-to-post I think still matters here. Double-Exalts are like storm serpent Lunars or full on isekai Getimians. Do what you will, but it's not something I think the setting will assume by default and not be written assuming as possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, I don't think that happenning to a ficticious person, that has not ever been not in destiny, is any different than having it happening to an alchemical recycled soul with full memories. Both of them have been 'born into being' and exalted.<br /> <br /> But ok, I won't belabor the point. Let's agree to disagree. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-18T11:33:07-08:00","id":1503391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontop</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1500752-understanding-liminals-and-getimians?p=1503380#post1503380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Eh, I don't think that happenning to a ficticious person, that has not ever been not in destiny, is any different than having it happening to an alchemical recycled soul with full memories. Both of them have been 'born into being' and exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>The soul stops being Exalted when it dies, and in the case of Luminous Exarch explicitly had a mortal in between.<br /> <br /> I mean, every single Exalt who has ever died in the setting has reincarnated into a mortal, barring some shenanigans that prevent them from reincarnating at all. An Alchemical who was formerly a Solar would be no different from a Solar who was formerly a Dragon Blood, or an Exigent who was formerly a Lunar, or any other case where that part of a person exits their dead meat and ends up inside a squalling newborn with its whole life ahead of it.<br /> <br /> And how full were the memories of Alchemicals supposed to be?<br /> <br /> I think Getimians are certainly different when their internal experience of themselves has a sense of continuity between existing in their Origin and it disappearing around them to be replaced by the reality that actually exists that coincides with the act of Exalting. It seems to me that there's an internal logic for Getimians that entails there being plausibility in them being Chosen, so it would be consistent in the fiction that their non-existent other life categorically could not have been Exalted as something else.<br /> <br /> The closest you can get to an Alchemical would be the case of a mortal who was possessed of some mysticism to know about prior lives and knew that their hun soul had previously belonged to an Exalt and was really on their high horse about it, and then when they come into existence as a Getimian frames it as being Twice Exalted in the same way that Exarch did.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-18T18:27:03-08:00","id":1503415,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s worth noting that Getimians have powers that draw upon and from their Origin, so one who was a powerful Exalt with resources unavailable to mortals or from a more technologically advanced alternate timeline might have a potential edge that they didn't pay for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-19T05:49:34-08:00","id":1503442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontop</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1500752-understanding-liminals-and-getimians?p=1503351#post1503351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could even have them coming from exaltations that never existed or that currently do not exist (that could get a good campaign seed that would be hard to do otherwise - 'I was an Auroral and now there are no Aurorals, why?' so this takes to investigating proscribed information about exalted, then about the Hearteaters, and so on).</div> </div> </div> </div>Returning to this.<br /> If I was the Storyteller I would probably ask why you were using a Getimian Exaltation as a springboard for this concept rather than playing the last Auroral.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>success is the ability to go from one failure to the next without any loss of enthusiasm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1115-the-hug-ninja","name":"The Hug Ninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1115_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"324"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-20T12:27:10-08:00","id":1503546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Hug Ninja</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1500752-understanding-liminals-and-getimians?p=1503442#post1503442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Returning to this.<br /> If I was the Storyteller I would probably ask why you were using a Getimian Exaltation as a springboard for this concept rather than playing the last Auroral.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you got the charmset?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-21T03:31:48-08:00","id":1503610,"title":"","content":"Well, either it's Ex3 and <i>we don't have the Getimian charmset yet either</i> or it's Exalted Essence and we don't need one to start with the Auroral charmset just some idea of Exalt Advantages and Anima Effects. Some modes would be nice, but you could also just as easily stick to the universal charms for your initial selection.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>success is the ability to go from one failure to the next without any loss of enthusiasm","edited":{"userid":1115,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1115-the-hug-ninja","user":"The Hug Ninja","date":". 02-21-2023, 03:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1115-the-hug-ninja","name":"The Hug Ninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1115_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"324"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-26T12:07:01-08:00","id":1503957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Hug Ninja</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1500752-understanding-liminals-and-getimians?p=1503610#post1503610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, either it's Ex3 and <i>we don't have the Getimian charmset yet either</i> or it's Exalted Essence and we don't need one to start with the Auroral charmset just some idea of Exalt Advantages and Anima Effects. Some modes would be nice, but you could also just as easily stick to the universal charms for your initial selection.</div> </div> </div> </div>Context of the discussion: I've added this short detour to Aurorals as a way to have something interesting from a Getimian ex-exalted. So yes, all I say is with the idea that it's when Getimians are released. Then, of course, it will come with the charmset.<br /> \u200b<br /> As for why creating Aurorals is not so desirable from my point of view: Having to heavily kitbash a partial charmset of a terrestrial-level sort-of-cousin on 3e, or just making a generic exalt and then doing all work on caste, charms and so is still a lot of work. Also, solo Aurorals have no context - no Auroral culture or recollection of history, no terrestrial gods know of them, Immaculate Order never heard of those. It's also harder to establish to the character how will they even know they are not some strange type of Exigence, let alone the fact that there could be a whole host of them.<br /> <br /> Getimian characters (will) have a complete charmset who are by design fishes-out-of-water who have personal stakes on how the world they see came to be so different, so they fit quite well.<br /> <br /> You know what would be another 'natural' way to establish a 'Hunt for Aurorals' plot? Playing a Hearteater. Of course, given the Hearteater nature, it would be a very different type of game than it'd be with Getimians.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-27T17:56:10-08:00","id":1504009,"title":"","content":"Similarly if we're reiterating context, this is about me considering it a red flag to ignore how destiny in 3rd edition and Getimian Origin's work. You can do whatever you like at your table.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>success is the ability to go from one failure to the next without any loss of enthusiasm","edited":{"userid":1115,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1115-the-hug-ninja","user":"The Hug Ninja","date":". 02-27-2023, 09:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1115-the-hug-ninja","name":"The Hug Ninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1115_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"324"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-02T09:45:58-08:00","id":1504206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Hug Ninja</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1500752-understanding-liminals-and-getimians?p=1504009#post1504009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Similarly if we're reiterating context, this is about me considering it a red flag to ignore how destiny in 3rd edition and Getimian Origin's work. You can do whatever you like at your table.</div> </div> </div> </div>Enlighten me. I'm bringing these quotes from Sidereals 3rd ed:<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;fate: The causal laws of Creation and Heaven. Fate dictates what futures \u2014 and destinies \u2014 <b>are possible</b>, defining the world\u2019s natural order&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;The Getimians truly are born of destinies that could have been, but the other Creations they claim to hail from \u2014 their Origins \u2014 <b>never existed</b>.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Getimian Charms snarl and tear at the threads of fate, infecting Creation with the <b>false reality of their Origins.</b>\u200b&quot;</i><br /> <br /> My conclusions:<br /> <br /> Getimian have never <b>existed </b>- so they have never been Exalted. Could have been, if they were not from a <b>false reality</b>.<br /> <br /> When the Getimians are brought to the true reality, they are unexalted, as they were not real, and then are exalted by this exact process that brought them to exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-02T12:48:54-08:00","id":1504220,"title":"","content":"Right, but only <i>mortals</i> are candidates for exaltation, so even some fictional, non-existent Solar can't be chosen to become a Getimian. Even if they aren't &quot;real&quot; outside of some god's discarded draft for the future - I won't bother asking why they're plotting out that sort of thing when Exalted are explicitly something to avoid there - they're already a Solar in there, and they don't get to be twice-chosen.\u200b<br /> <br /> Unless you want them to, this is just play-pretend make believe, do as you like with <i>your</i> buds at <i>your</i> table, etc, etc, etc.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26730-tomdick-harry","name":"TomDick&Harry","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-06T10:34:24-08:00","id":1504611,"title":"","content":"So people with the Essence book and/or access to the Discord, would you pretty please provide some more detail about Liminals, Getimians, and Exigents?<br /> <br /> 1. Who/what is the Dark Mother?<br /> 2. What purpose did she make the Liminals for, and why during the Shogunate?<br /> 3. Please share, what are the new versions of the Aspects?* What type of origin does each have? What are their animas and aspect markings like?<br /> 4. What kind of martial arts, sorcery, and necromancy can they access?<br /> \u200b5. How many Liminals are there in the Time of Tumult?<br /> <br /> *This is what I have seen before about them, posted by ??? (long version) and I don't know anything about &quot;Alex Mercer&quot; so that wasn't a helpful example.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Flesh Aspects</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"> like Mercer are created by those motivated by vengeance; they're stitching corpses together to create weapons to destroy their enemies. The original Alex Mercer unleashed Blacklight to spite and hurt Blackwatch and humanity in general, and accidentally created his greatest possible weapon against both. Charms of the Flesh Aspect not only allow for more efficient cannibalism, but also for feats of physical, muscular power and athleticism.<br /> <br /> <b>Blood Aspects</b> are created by those motivated by lust or similarly possessive emotions. Dame Crimson, the signature Blood Aspect, was stitched together from a number of priestesses that served a Forest King. The god murdered them all because they each had some imperfection that displeased him, and he tried to combine them all into a single perfect priestess. Instead, he got Dame Crimson, who murdered him right back. Possibly related, she goes on to seduce another god's priest, which is appropriate to the lusty nature of Blood Aspect Chernozem. Charms of this Aspect can track people through blood, manipulate blood-born diseases, and navigate waters, among other fluid talents.<br /> <br /> <b>Marrow Aspects</b> are created by those motivated by scientific curiosity; they're more interested in the process and the art than in the specific result. [Presumably like Dr. Frankenstein.] Likewise, Chernozem of this Aspect are talented at delving into secrets. Oh, and they can manipulate bones, giving themselves sharp weapons and hard armor.<br /> <br /> <b>Breath Aspects</b> are created by those motivated by sheer nihilism -- I guess from a desire to destroy the world or desecrate the dead? Either way, these Chernozem are good at manipulating air and blending in with humans.<br /> <br /> <b>Soil Aspects</b> are created by those motivated by sorrow and regret -- a lover trying to bring back his best friend rather than his sex-pal, or perhaps a parent (or child) looking to bring back his child (or parent). These Chernozem are best at raising and controlling zombies, as well as reading omens and seeing prophecies.</span> </div> </div> </div></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> 6. Please describe the Castes of Getimians? I know they have been described, but I know nothing about them except names. What kind of &quot;people&quot; are they Chosen from, what are their animas and caste marks?<br /> 7. When and how did Oramus and the Lidless Eye make them? What for? I saw a quote about those Titans having access to a place where Exaltations were locked up or sealed, but what does that mean?<br /> 8. When did Rakan Thulio find or revive the Getimians?<br /> 9. Is it canon there are exactly 64 Getimians?<br /> <br /> 10. How many Exigents are there in the Time of Tumult? Are there any numbers given for the &quot;groups&quot; of them like Architects and Sovereigns?<br /> <br /> 11. Who are the named canonical NPCs of these three splats? I know of some names but I don't know their castes/aspects, nor if any more have been made canon, or really any details about them besides Strawmaiden Janest and the brief mentions in the old old previews from the Ex3 KS.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 03-06-2023, 02:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-06T11:41:46-08:00","id":1504617,"title":"","content":"I suppose this is the thread to ask questions about this:-<br /> <br /> One of the things in 3E was the act of creating Exalts REDUCED the being involved.<br /> <br /> It's why gods get weaker or die when they create Exigents.<br /> <br /> Even the UCS was weakened when he created the Solars.<br /> <br /> My question regarding Liminels and Getimains is whether this assumption is still valid for them?<br /> <br /> Are the primordials who made them getting reduced in the same way?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4678-tryingtobeslim","name":"TryingToBeSlim","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-06T12:43:15-08:00","id":1504621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1500752-understanding-liminals-and-getimians?p=1504611#post1504611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> ...<br /> 1. Who/what is the Dark Mother?</div> </div> </div> </div>Some Underworld entity that seems to want to reinforce the barrier of life and death, who predates the Divine Revolution. That's about all we know honeslty.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1500752-understanding-liminals-and-getimians?p=1504611#post1504611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. What purpose did she make the Liminals for, and why during the Shogunate?</div> </div> </div> </div>We don't know a lot about her. She made them to basically again, enforce the barriers of life and death. She tends to try to communicate more through like, atavistic impulses, dreams, and stuff of her Chosen. Why the Shoguante is implied to do maybe with the rise of the Deathlords, but again, all we know is she didn't have Exalts until then.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1500752-understanding-liminals-and-getimians?p=1504611#post1504611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3. Please share, what are the new versions of the Aspects?* What type of origin does each have? What are their animas and aspect markings like?</div> </div> </div> </div>Their Aspects are more or less as in the 3e corebook: Blood, Breath, Flesh, Marrow, Soil. The main thing that results in their Aspect is kind of the emotional resonance of whomever was trying ot create them. Their Aspect markings and anima reflect this as well.<ul><li>Children of Blood result from desire, greed, and ambition. They tend to become pale, eyes become full with blood and dark water begins to drip from their body. Think a drowning victim I guess.</li> <li>Children of Breath are from regret or repentence. Aspect markings involve pale skin, foul winds, and their voice seeming quieter. I think the vibes are someone who's suffocated.</li> <li>Children of Flesh are from rage and vengeance. When they spend too much Essence the patchwork nature of their bodies become more obvious, with stiches becoming more pronounced and ichor oozing between gaps.The vibe I get is the corpse going all-out.</li> <li>Chidlren of Marrow are from curiousity and obssession. The description of their markings is akin to dessicaiton. Think how hair and nails and teeth become more pronounced as rigor mortus kicks in.</li> <li>Children of Soil are born from sorrow and yearning. Their bodies become covered in grave dirt and things like worms or other aspects of rot show through.</li> </ul><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1500752-understanding-liminals-and-getimians?p=1504611#post1504611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4. What kind of martial arts, sorcery, and necromancy can they access?</div> </div> </div> </div>They are on in the same assumed &quot;area of play&quot; as Dragon-Blooded. So they deal with Terrestrial keyword with Martial Arts, can access Ivory Circle Necromancy, sometimes Terrestrial Circle Sorcery instead. They are as per <i>Arms of the Chosen</i> neutral with soulsteel and Dissonant with other materials, again, as per usal for most Exalts meant for Terrestrial play.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1500752-understanding-liminals-and-getimians?p=1504611#post1504611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b5. How many Liminals are there in the Time of Tumult?</div> </div> </div> </div>Last it came up a couple years ago from devs around 250, but this is subject to change or never be brought-up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1500752-understanding-liminals-and-getimians?p=1504611#post1504611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">6. Please describe the Castes of Getimians? I know they have been described, but I know nothing about them except names. What kind of &quot;people&quot; are they Chosen from, what are their animas and caste marks?</div> </div> </div> </div>The general thing is the actions that would have made them worthy of Exaltation in their Origins determines their Caste. The Castes are:<ul><li>Spring - Brought beauty to the world in some way. Typically chairsmatic, inspiring, exemplary.</li> <li>Summer - Brought change to their world thorugh some form of conquest. War, religious reform, coups, revolutions, rebellions, that sort of thing.</li> <li>Autumn brought change to their Origins in some way that helped others. Saving the meek, protecting the weak, curing the sick. They sacrificed their time and energy to make other's lives better.</li> <li>Winter did something to the world thorugh mystic force or reformation of socieites. New academic paradigms, being sorcerer-kings, educating the masses, bringing major cultural reform.</li> </ul>Their Castemarks and such are rendered here in order. Spoilered tos ave space.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <img width=\"1625\" height=\"500\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/Xc5zojN.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/Xc5zojN.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/Xc5zojN.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1500752-understanding-liminals-and-getimians?p=1504611#post1504611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">7. When and how did Oramus and the Lidless Eye make them? What for? I saw a quote about those Titans having access to a place where Exaltations were locked up or sealed, but what does that mean?</div> </div> </div> </div>During the Divine Revolution. They tried it see what they woudl get or if it might help. THey didn't like what htey got out of it and so boxed them away into Zen Mu. Zen Mu is something from 2e originally but think of it like, this prototype/test server thing before the Ancients went to make Creation proper. It also happens to be where they stashed stuff they forgot about.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1500752-understanding-liminals-and-getimians?p=1504611#post1504611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">8. When did Rakan Thulio find or revive the Getimians?</div> </div> </div> </div>Within the last century.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1500752-understanding-liminals-and-getimians?p=1504611#post1504611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">9. Is it canon there are exactly 64 Getimians?</div> </div> </div> </div>It hasn't been stated either way in actual print but is intent of at least one dev.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1500752-understanding-liminals-and-getimians?p=1504611#post1504611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">10. How many Exigents are there in the Time of Tumult? Are there any numbers given for the &quot;groups&quot; of them like Architects and Sovereigns?</div> </div> </div> </div>Less than Lunars, more than Sidereals as per their book. &quot;As many as needed&quot; for those groups, but likely not more than a dozen of any particular sort, if that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1500752-understanding-liminals-and-getimians?p=1504611#post1504611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">11. Who are the named canonical NPCs of these three splats? I know of some names but I don't know their castes/aspects, nor if any more have been made canon, or really any details about them besides Strawmaiden Janest and the brief mentions in the old old previews from the Ex3 KS.</div> </div> </div> </div>No sigs have been detailed for Liminals and Getimians yet. The characers in the Essence art are not meant to be representative of any either. Janest is the de facto general Exigents sig, plus we have had a few other named exmaple ones, and token example Sovereign and Architects in the fiction, namely the Architect of Wu Jian has shown-up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-06T12:47:46-08:00","id":1504622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TryingToBeSlim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1500752-understanding-liminals-and-getimians?p=1504617#post1504617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...<br /> My question regarding Liminels and Getimains is whether this assumption is still valid for them?<br /> <br /> Are the primordials who made them getting reduced in the same way?</div> </div> </div> </div>For Getimians and Oramus and Sacvherell, we don't know. All signs point to yes, though. Note that they may not be actively diminished now as thier Exaltation is the sort of thing that perpetuates probably. SOmething I tend to think on is every possible Getimian ever in the future is already Chosen. This is a fun bit with the combination of the two titans invovled being Laplace's Demon and the Ultimate Wave Form Observer.<br /> <br /> The Dark Mother is presumebly diminished also, but we know so little on her we can't say what it did and it's apparent enough she's on par with the Incarna and Dragons that she can keep Exalting a whole hsot instead of a single Exaltation with an Exigence boost doing them in pretty bad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-06T13:16:06-08:00","id":1504626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1500752-understanding-liminals-and-getimians?p=1504611#post1504611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So people with the Essence book and/or access to the Discord, would you pretty please provide some more detail about Liminals, Getimians, and Exigents?<br /> <br /> 1. Who/what is the Dark Mother?<br /> 2. What purpose did she make the Liminals for, and why during the Shogunate?<br /> 3. Please share, what are the new versions of the Aspects?* What type of origin does each have? What are their animas and aspect markings like?<br /> 4. What kind of martial arts, sorcery, and necromancy can they access?<br /> \u200b5. How many Liminals are there in the Time of Tumult?</div> </div> </div> </div>1) An ancient power of the Underworld, from dev commentary originating before the Neverborn crashed in.<br /> 2) She makes them to fortify the lines between living and dead. Why she started - and why she started <i>when</i> she started - is unknown.<br /> 3) Nothing's changed on the Aspects and their origins - i.e., the driving emotions of their creators - since the 3e core, although I would summarise them as Blood Aspects being the products of desire, greed and ambition (you want them, you want status, you want money, you <i>want)</i>, Breath being the product of regret and repentance (you made a mistake, and this is how you'll make up for it), Flesh being the product of rage and vengeance (you're pissed off about something; they're the most likely to have their creator be the &quot;I'll show them all&quot; type), Marrow being the product of curiosity and obsession (c.f. Frankenstein), and Soil being the product of sorrow and yearning (you feel their loss, feel their absence, you wish they could come back).<br /> <br /> Their general animas are gruesome and numinous displays of blood, muscle and soil, and their general aspect markings reveal them as patchwork corpses. Blood Aspects' specific markings are pallid skin, red eyes, and dark water dripping from their bodies, Breath Aspects' are bluish skin and lips, and a raspy voice, Flesh Aspects' are more visible - and more straining - stitching as their wounds ooze black pus, Marrow Aspects' are a desiccated body and unnaturally long teeth and nails, and Soil Aspects' are grave dirt coating their skin with worms writhing in their eyes and mouth<br /> 4) They use the Terrestrial mode on Martial Arts. They can learn First Circle Necromancy, and a rare few can learn First Circle Sorcery, but they can't learn both.<br /> 5) Nothing official as yet, but about 200 or so gets passed around.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1500752-understanding-liminals-and-getimians?p=1504611#post1504611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">6. Please describe the Castes of Getimians? I know they have been described, but I know nothing about them except names. What kind of &quot;people&quot; are they Chosen from, what are their animas and caste marks?<br /> 7. When and how did Oramus and the Lidless Eye make them? What for? I saw a quote about those Titans having access to a place where Exaltations were locked up or sealed, but what does that mean?<br /> 8. When did Rakan Thulio find or revive the Getimians?<br /> 9. Is it canon there are exactly 64 Getimians?</div> </div> </div> </div>6) Spring Castes are warrior-poets, guardians, and idealists. Summer Castes are conquerors, iconclasts, and visionary prophets. Autumn Castes are saviors, healers, and inspiring war-leaders. Winter Castes are magicians, demiurges and power brokers. Their caste marks are the astrological signs for the asteroids Juno, Pallas, Ceres, and Vesta respectively; their baseline animas are pale colors mixed with black and white, with Spring being pink, Summer being grass-green, Autumn being orange, and Winter being gray blue, expanding to visions from their Origin with pattern spiders scuttling within at iconic.<br /> 7) During the Divine Revolution (the Primordial War). As yet, we don't know why they did it. The reference you came across is probably to the Getimian Exaltations being sealed away in Zen-Mu shortly after their creation, but full details on that will have to wait.<br /> 8) He appears to have found the Getimian Exaltations about fifty years prior to the present, per the Sidereals manuscript.<br /> 9) Not given in print yet, but it'll probably be the finalised number,<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1500752-understanding-liminals-and-getimians?p=1504611#post1504611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">10. How many Exigents are there in the Time of Tumult? Are there any numbers given for the &quot;groups&quot; of them like Architects and Sovereigns?</div> </div> </div> </div>10) Somewhere in the low two hundreds.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-06T17:25:53-08:00","id":1504678,"title":"","content":"Thank you so much Marin, that's great! The part about Zen-Mu is especially interesting -- it suggests Rakan Thulio may have travelled there. Maybe he used that gate in the Southeast.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1500752-understanding-liminals-and-getimians?p=1504626#post1504626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) She makes them to fortify the lines between living and dead. Why she started - and why she started <i>when</i> she started - is unknown.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThe lines dividing the living and dead, or the lines connecting them?<br /> <br /> <br /> I have another question, I'm guessing nobody knows this one but here goes:<br /> <br /> We know that when an Alchemical is created, they receive a hun soul that already existed. Is this the case with Liminals and/or Getimians, or do they start with completely new human souls? I feel like it would make sense for Liminals to reincarnate an existing human soul, and Getimians to get new ones.<br /> <br /> Also, does anyone know yet if Liminals or Getimians can have children with mortals? I assume Getimians can, but Liminals are kinda undead-ish so I wonder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 03-06-2023, 09:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-06T19:15:59-08:00","id":1504701,"title":"","content":"Note that 3e is depreciating the use of the Mandarin for the higher and lower souls. Things in the corebook of that sort are kind of legacy code.<br /> <br /> And on Liminals no clue. We don't honeslty know enough of them metaphysically on that front. On children, also no clue. Not something that's been relevant. The topic may or may not come up in their book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-07T00:01:56-08:00","id":1504734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1500752-understanding-liminals-and-getimians?p=1504678#post1504678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bThe lines dividing the living and dead, or the lines connecting them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Dividing. They're intended to keep the living and the dead separate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-10T07:39:47-08:00","id":1505017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1500752-understanding-liminals-and-getimians?p=1502698#post1502698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> So, fun fact:<br /> <br /> Holden has been putting out an &quot;Exalted demake,&quot; which is to say, Exalted rendered in oWoD 20th anniversary mechanics. I happened to snag his preview of Liminals, built on the same ideas that went into the old Kickstarter preview -- Liminals as they were to be, rather than how they will be -- and they're really just Prometheans.<br /> <br /> Though they are hunters of the dead and aligned with the Underworld, they also have pretty half-cocked alchemical theming (mostly arbitrary alchemical terms in various Charm names) and a mechanic and play loop for &quot;the Journey&quot; to leave the Liminal condition behind, becoming instead a mortal or a personal kind of Exalted.<br /> <br /> I suspect the new writing team are going to take them in a different direction.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a few details in the demake that don't 100% align with stuff I and others were told during Ex3's development. It's probably the most glaring with Infernals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-11T06:31:58-08:00","id":1505111,"title":"","content":"I have a feeling that writing something for a personal project like this would go out of its way to not make them how they were intended to be for publication.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-11T07:30:39-08:00","id":1505114,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it was also almost a decade ago and opinions and inspirations change in that time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}